  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq700.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 716.05 Sludge Storage Requirements",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 716.05 Sludge Storage Requirements.\n\n(a) Sludge storage facilities shall be designed to control odors so that odors do not create a nuisance at the property boundary.\n\n(b) Storage capacity shall be designed to accommodate at least 5 days of sludge production based on maximum month design sludge generation rate.\n\n(c) Storage areas shall be designed to minimize tracking of dewatered cake on-site and eliminate runoff from the dewatered cake storage area to other portions of the site or off-site.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Wq 700) #8590, eff 3-25-06; ss by #10693, eff 10-15-14; ss by #14258, eff 7-1-25, EXPIRES: 7-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq700.html"
